{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015qU88NAxVLbZzZ11h32L2r","type":"tool_result","content":"I appreciate your request, but I need to note that the web page content you provided doesn't actually contain the \"Three Big Concepts\" list (Charts, Repository, Release definitions) that you're asking me to quote as item A. That content appears to be from a different page—likely the \"Introduction to Helm\" page mentioned in the navigation.\n\nFrom the page provided, I can accurately quote:\n\n**B)** \"Now the `wordpress` chart is installed. Note that installing a chart creates a new _release_ object.\" And: \"If you want Helm to generate a name for you, leave off the release name and use `--generate-name`.\"\n\n**C)** \"*   `--values` (or `-f`): Specify a YAML file with overrides. This can be specified multiple times and the rightmost file will take precedence\n*   `--set`: Specify overrides on the command line.\n\nIf both are used, `--set` values are merged into `--values` with higher precedence.\"\n\n**D)** (i) \"It will only update things that have changed since the last release.\"\n(ii) \"`helm rollback [RELEASE] [REVISION]`\"\n(iii) \"A release version is an incremental revision. Every time an install, upgrade, or rollback happens, the revision number is incremented by 1.\"\n(iv) \"we can use `helm history [RELEASE]` to see revision numbers for a certain release.\"\n(v) \"If a release was created by a rollback, pass `--show-rollback-revision` to `helm history`...\"\n\n**E)** \"`helm uninstall happy-panda`\" and \"If you wish to keep a deletion release record, use `helm uninstall --keep-history`.\"\n\nFor item A, you'll need to consult the Introduction to Helm page."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ba092422-5310-41aa-b517-7e6c04f864c8","uuid":"1e8c1b16-b257-458e-b11e-cfe2b7dde36c","timestamp":"2026-08-31T08:28:30.672Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":78660,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"I appreciate your request, but I