{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01R8di5wrk97YUbPZJtXbqyX","type":"tool_result","content":"# Helm Chart Repository Guide - Key Definitions\n\n## Chart Repository Definition\n\nAccording to Helm's documentation, \"A _chart repository_ is an HTTP server that houses an `index.yaml` file and optionally some packaged charts.\"\n\nThe guide further explains that \"a chart repository can be any HTTP server that can serve YAML and tar files and can answer GET requests.\"\n\n## Repository Structure\n\nA chart repository consists of:\n- Packaged charts (`.tgz` files)\n- A special `index.yaml` file containing an index of all charts\n\nExample layout:\n```\ncharts/\n  |- index.yaml\n  |- alpine-0.1.2.tgz\n  |- alpine-0.1.2.tgz.prov\n```\n\n## Index File\n\nThe `index.yaml` is a YAML file containing metadata about packaged charts, including information from each chart's `Chart.yaml` file. \"A valid chart repository must have an index file.\"\n\n## Essential Commands\n\n- `helm repo add [NAME] [URL]` - adds a repository\n- `helm repo list` - displays configured repositories\n- `helm repo update` - fetches latest chart information\n- `helm repo index [PATH] --url [URL]` - generates an index file\n- `helm package [CHART-NAME]/` - packages a chart\n\n## Key Note\n\n\"A repository will not be added if it does not contain a valid `index.yaml`.\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ba092422-5310-41aa-b517-7e6c04f864c8","uuid":"af69cf5a-2882-4242-8567-3e92ea426abc","timestamp":"2026-08-31T08:28:43.420Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":62459,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Helm Chart Repository Guide - Key Definitions\n\n## Chart Repository Definition\n\nAccording to Helm's documentation, \"A _chart repository_ is an HTTP server that houses an `index.yaml` file and optionally some packaged charts.\"\n\nThe guide further explains that \"a chart repository can be any HTTP server that can serve YAML and tar files and can answer GET requests.\"\n\n## Repository Structure\n\nA chart repository consists of:\n- Packaged charts (`.tgz` files)\n- A special `index.yaml` file containing an index of all charts\n\nExample layout:\n```\ncharts/\n  |- index.yaml\n  |- alpine-0.1.2.tgz\n  |- alpine-0.1.2.tgz.prov\n```\n\n## Index File\n\nThe `index.yaml` is a YAML file containing metadata about packaged charts, including information from each chart's `Chart.yaml` file. \"A valid chart repository must have an index file.\"\n\n## Essential Commands\n\n- `helm repo add [NAME] [URL]` - adds a repository\n- `helm repo list` - displays configured repositories\n- `helm repo update` - fetches latest chart information\n- `helm repo index [PATH] --url [URL]` - generates an index file\n- `helm package [CHART-NAME]/` - packages a chart\n\n## Key Note\n\n\"A repository will not be added if it does not contain a valid `index.yaml`.\"","durationMs":4739,"url":"https://helm.sh/docs/topics/chart_repository/"}}
