ment\n    name: my-app\n  patch: |-\n    - op: replace\n      path: /spec/replicas\n      value: 3\n    - op: add\n      path: /spec/template/spec/containers/0/env/-\n      value:\n        name: ENV_VAR\n        value: value\n```\n\n#### Images\n\nYou can change images in a kustomization without creating patches. Use the `images` field to list all images you want to replace:\n\n```yaml\nimages:\n- name: my-app\n  newName: my-app\n  newTag: v2\n```\n\n#### Replicas\n\nYou can override the number of replicas for Deployments and StatefulSets using the `replicas` field:\n\n```yaml\nreplicas:\n- name: my-app\n  count: 3\n```\n\n## Bases and Overlays\n\nKustomize supports a \"base and overlay\" concept. A **base** is a kustomization directory which contains a set of resources and a kustomization.yaml file. A base can be either a local directory or a directory from a remote repo. The **overlay** is a kustomization directory which references other kustomization directories and applies additional customization on top of them.\n\nHere's an example directory structure:\n\n```\nmy-app/\n├── base/\n│   ├── deployment.yaml\n│   ├── service.yaml\n│   └── kustomization.yaml\n├── overlays/\n│   ├── dev/\n│   │   ├── kustomization.yaml\n│   │   └── dev-patch.yaml\n│   └── prod/\n│       ├── kustomization.yaml\n│       └── prod-patch.yaml\n```\n\nThe `base/kustomization.yaml` contains:\n\n```yaml\nresources:\n- deployment.yaml\n- service.yaml\n```\n\nThe `overlays/dev/kustomization.yaml` contains:\n\n```yaml\nbases:\n- ../../base\npatchesStrategicMerge:\n- dev-patch.yaml\nnamePrefix: dev-\n```\n\nThe `overlays/prod/kustomization.yaml` contains:\n\n```yaml\nbases:\n- ../../base\npatchesStrategicMerge:\n- prod-patch.yaml\nnamePrefix: prod-\nreplicas:\n- name: my-app\n  count: 3\n```\n\n## How to apply/view/delete objects using Kustomize\n\nTo view resources found in a directory containing a kustomization file, run:\n\n```shell\nkubectl kustomize <kustomization_directory>\n```\n\nTo view