{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RnNTNSbZimggu6REE9SLvm","type":"tool_result","content":"# Helm OCI Registry Documentation\n\n## Opening Overview\n\n\"It is recommended to use container registries with [OCI](https://www.opencontainers.org/) support to store and share chart packages.\"\n\nThe documentation does not explicitly state which Helm version made OCI support the default or generally available.\n\n## OCI Artifacts and Chart References\n\n\"An OCI-based registry can contain zero or more Helm repositories and each of those repositories can contain zero or more packaged Helm charts.\"\n\n\"When using `helm push` to upload a chart an OCI registry, the reference must be prefixed with `oci://` and must not contain the basename or tag.\"\n\n## Core Commands\n\n**Push Command:**\n```\n$ helm push mychart-0.1.0.tgz oci://localhost:5000/helm-charts\n```\n\n**Pull Command:**\n```\n$ helm pull oci://localhost:5000/helm-charts/mychart --version 0.1.0\n```\n\n**Install Command:**\n```\n$ helm install myrelease oci://localhost:5000/helm-charts/mychart --version 0.1.0\n```\n\n**Registry Login/Logout:**\n```\n$ helm registry login -u myuser localhost:5000\n$ helm registry logout localhost:5000\n```\n\n**Show Command:**\n```\n$ helm show all oci://localhost:5000/helm-charts/mychart --version 0.1.0\n```\n\n## Chart Naming and Versioning\n\n\"The registry reference basename is inferred from the chart's name, and the tag is inferred from the chart's semantic version.\"\n\n## Key Limitation\n\nThe documentation does not include a dedicated \"Where are my charts?\" section, nor does it mention that `helm repo add` doesn't work with OCI registries."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ba092422-5310-41aa-b517-7e6c04f864c8","uuid":"d6c9e7c7-0629-478e-95bf-a7f3b3687684","timestamp":"2026-08-31T08:28:48.657Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":61573,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Helm OCI Registry Documentation\n\n## Opening Overview\n\n\"It is recommended to use container registries with [OCI](https://www.opencontainers.org/) support to store and share chart packages.\"\n\nThe documentation does not explicitly state which Helm version made OCI support the default or generally available.\n\n## OCI Artifacts and Chart References\n\n\"An OCI-based registry can contain zero or more Helm repositories and each of those repositories can contain zero or more packaged Helm charts.\"\n\n\"When using `helm push` to upload a chart an OCI registry, the reference must be prefixed with `oci://` and must not contain the basename or tag.\"\n\n## Core Commands\n\n**Push Command:**\n```\n$ helm push mychart-0.1.0.tgz oci://localhost:5000/helm-charts\n```\n\n**Pull Command:**\n```\n$ helm pull oci://localhost:5000/helm-charts/mychart --version 0.1.0\n```\n\n**Install Command:**\n```\n$ helm install myrelease oci://localhost:5000/helm-charts/mychart --version 0.1.0\n```\n\n**Registry Login/Logout:**\n```\n$ helm registry login -u myuser localhost:5000\n$ helm registry logout localhost:5000\n```\n\n**Show Command:**\n```\n$ helm show all oci://localhost:5000/helm-charts/mychart --version 0.1.0\n```\n\n## Chart Naming and Versioning\n\n\"The registry reference basename is inferred from the chart's name, and the tag is inferred from the chart's semantic version.\"\n\n## Key Limitation\n\nThe documentation does not include a dedicated \"Where are my charts?\" section, nor does it mention that `helm repo add` doesn't work with OCI registries.","durationMs":5193,"url":"https://helm.sh/docs/topics/registries/"}}
