{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Jjcsyfw1Cfs4J5BjMFunyW","type":"tool_result","content":"# Helm Custom Resource Definitions - Documentation Summary\n\nPer the Helm documentation (CC-BY-4.0), here are the key points about CRD management:\n\n## Two Distinct Components\nThe documentation distinguishes between:\n- A CRD declaration (YAML with kind `CustomResourceDefinition`)\n- Resources that use the CRD (resources with the CRD's apiVersion and kind)\n\n## Method 1: Built-in CRD Directory\nHelm 3+ introduced a `crds/` directory in charts where:\n- CRDs are placed but not templated\n- They install automatically via `helm install`\n- Use `--skip-crds` flag to skip installation\n- Existing CRDs are skipped with a warning\n\n**Key Limitation**: As the documentation states, \"There is no support at this time for upgrading or deleting CRDs using Helm.\"\n\n## Important Caveats\n\nThe documentation explicitly notes:\n- CRD upgrades and deletions are unsupported\n- `--dry-run` doesn't work with CRDs (can't validate CRs without CRD installed)\n- CRDs cannot be templated (to maintain chart validation integrity)\n\n## Method 2: Separate Charts\nAlternative approach using distinct charts—one for CRD declarations, another for CRD-using resources. Requires separate installation but suits cluster operators with admin access.\n\nThis reflects Helm's deliberate design prioritizing safety over automation for CRD lifecycle management."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ba092422-5310-41aa-b517-7e6c04f864c8","uuid":"3c0083ad-2f55-4d1f-bf98-69c6733cc83c","timestamp":"2026-08-31T08:29:24.265Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":32934,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Helm Custom Resource Definitions - Documentation Summary\n\nPer the Helm documentation (CC-BY-4.0), here are the key points about CRD management:\n\n## Two Distinct Components\nThe documentation distinguishes between:\n- A CRD declaration (YAML with kind `CustomResourceDefinition`)\n- Resources that use the CRD (resources with the CRD's apiVersion and kind)\n\n## Method 1: Built-in CRD Directory\nHelm 3+ introduced a `crds/` directory in charts where:\n- CRDs are placed but not templated\n- They install automatically via `helm install`\n- Use `--skip-crds` flag to skip installation\n- Existing CRDs are skipped with a warning\n\n**Key Limitation**: As the documentation states, \"There is no support at this time for upgrading or deleting CRDs using Helm.\"\n\n## Important Caveats\n\nThe documentation explicitly notes:\n- CRD upgrades and deletions are unsupported\n- `--dry-run` doesn't work with CRDs (can't validate CRs without CRD installed)\n- CRDs cannot be templated (to maintain chart validation integrity)\n\n## Method 2: Separate Charts\nAlternative approach using distinct charts—one for CRD declarations, another for CRD-using resources. Requires separate installation but suits cluster operators with admin access.\n\nThis reflects Helm's deliberate design prioritizing safety over automation for CRD lifecycle management.","durationMs":5119,"url":"https://helm.sh/docs/chart_best_practices/custom_resource_definitions/"}}
