{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SZ8SxgbMycMaZ4HagARYic","type":"tool_result","content":"# Storage Backends Section\n\nHere's the storage backends content from the Helm documentation:\n\n**Default Storage:**\n\"By default, release information is stored in Secrets in the namespace of the release.\"\n\n**Environment Variable:**\nThe `HELM_DRIVER` environment variable controls backend selection and accepts these values: `[configmap, secret, sql]`.\n\n**ConfigMap Backend:**\nSet the environment variable with `export HELM_DRIVER=configmap`. The documentation warns that ConfigMap storage may expose sensitive data (passwords, keys, credentials) that Secrets would normally protect, since Kubernetes RBAC typically restricts Secret access more strictly.\n\n**SQL Backend:**\nThis is marked as beta and stores release information in SQL databases. It's useful when release data exceeds 1MB, which would violate Kubernetes etcd limits.\n\nConfiguration requires:\n```\nexport HELM_DRIVER=sql\nexport HELM_DRIVER_SQL_CONNECTION_STRING=postgresql://helm-postgres:5432/helm?user=helm&password=changeme\n```\n\nCurrently, only PostgreSQL is supported. The documentation recommends enabling permission management to mirror Kubernetes RBAC for release information."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ba092422-5310-41aa-b517-7e6c04f864c8","uuid":"34c5414a-85fb-442d-9a19-d43af836e58b","timestamp":"2026-08-31T08:30:50.179Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":53020,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Storage Backends Section\n\nHere's the storage backends content from the Helm documentation:\n\n**Default Storage:**\n\"By default, release information is stored in Secrets in the namespace of the release.\"\n\n**Environment Variable:**\nThe `HELM_DRIVER` environment variable controls backend selection and accepts these values: `[configmap, secret, sql]`.\n\n**ConfigMap Backend:**\nSet the environment variable with `export HELM_DRIVER=configmap`. The documentation warns that ConfigMap storage may expose sensitive data (passwords, keys, credentials) that Secrets would normally protect, since Kubernetes RBAC typically restricts Secret access more strictly.\n\n**SQL Backend:**\nThis is marked as beta and stores release information in SQL databases. It's useful when release data exceeds 1MB, which would violate Kubernetes etcd limits.\n\nConfiguration requires:\n```\nexport HELM_DRIVER=sql\nexport HELM_DRIVER_SQL_CONNECTION_STRING=postgresql://helm-postgres:5432/helm?user=helm&password=changeme\n```\n\nCurrently, only PostgreSQL is supported. The documentation recommends enabling permission management to mirror Kubernetes RBAC for release information.","durationMs":4451,"url":"https://helm.sh/docs/topics/advanced/"}}
