{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Tizt1YjZR15w5tzXxG1aeF","type":"tool_result","content":"# Answers About Helm Page Content\n\n1. **What is a \"release\" and what happens when you install a chart?**\n\n   \"Installing a chart creates a new _release_ object.\"\n\n2. **Can the same chart be installed more than once into the same cluster?**\n\n   Yes, this is demonstrated in the example where the user can use `--generate-name` or provide different release names. The text shows \"If you want Helm to generate a name for you, leave off the release name and use `--generate-name`,\" implying multiple installations are possible.\n\n3. **Exact `helm rollback` usage line shown:**\n\n   `helm rollback happy-panda 1`\n\n4. **What is a release version/revision and when is it incremented?**\n\n   \"A release version is an incremental revision. Every time an install, upgrade, or rollback happens, the revision number is incremented by 1.\"\n\n5. **What does `helm history` show?**\n\n   \"we can use `helm history [RELEASE]` to see revision numbers for a certain release.\"\n\n6. **Revision numbers in the worked example:**\n\n   No `helm history` output block is provided in the page. The page only mentions `helm history` as a command without showing example output.\n\n7. **What does the page say about `helm uninstall --keep-history`?**\n\n   \"If you wish to keep a deletion release record, use `helm uninstall --keep-history`.\"\n\n8. **Difference between `--set` and `-f`/`--values`, and which wins?**\n\n   \"If both are used, `--set` values are merged into `--values` with higher precedence.\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ba092422-5310-41aa-b517-7e6c04f864c8","uuid":"213f7d41-4727-4fe7-b20e-4d2384504a72","timestamp":"2026-08-31T08:31:13.730Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":78660,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Answers About Helm Page Content\n\n1. **What is a \"release\" and what happens when you install a chart?**\n\n   \"Installing a chart creates a new _release_ object.\"\n\n2. **Can the same chart be installed more than once into the same cluster?**\n\n   Yes, this is demonstrated in the example where the user can use `--generate-name` or provide different release names. The text shows \"If you want Helm to generate a name for you, leave off the release name and use `--generate-name`,\" implying multiple installations are possible.\n\n3. **Exact `helm rollback` usage line shown:**\n\n   `helm rollback happy-panda 1`\n\n4. **What is a release version/revision and when is it incremented?**\n\n   \"A release version is an incremental revision. Every time an install, upgrade, or rollback happens, the revision number is incremented by 1.\"\n\n5. **What does `helm history` show?**\n\n   \"we can use `helm history [RELEASE]` to see revision numbers for a certain release.\"\n\n6. **Revision numbers in the worked example:**\n\n   No `helm history` output block is provided in the page. The page only mentions `helm history` as a command without showing example output.\n\n7. **What does the page say about `helm uninstall --keep-history`?**\n\n   \"If you wish to keep a deletion release record, use `helm uninstall --keep-history`.\"\n\n8. **Difference between `--set` and `-f`/`--values`, and which wins?**\n\n   \"If both are used, `--set` values are merged into `--values` with higher precedence.\"","durationMs":4844,"url":"https://helm.sh/docs/intro/using_helm/"}}
