{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0157P6J9ojyTF8MRbSLhyCTS","type":"tool_result","content":"# Glossary Terms from Helm Documentation\n\n**Chart**\n\"A Helm package that contains information sufficient for installing a set of Kubernetes resources into a Kubernetes cluster.\"\n\n**Chart Archive**\n\"A _chart archive_ is a tarred and gzipped (and optionally signed) chart.\"\n\n**Chart Dependency (Subcharts)**\nCharts may depend on other charts through soft dependencies (not requiring Helm tooling) or hard dependencies (bundled within the `charts/` directory and installed together).\n\n**Chart Version**\n\"Charts are versioned according to the [SemVer 2 spec](https://semver.org). A version number is required on every chart.\"\n\n**Chart.yaml**\n\"Information about a chart is stored in a special file called `Chart.yaml`. Every chart must have this file.\"\n\n**Helm (and helm)**\nHelm is the Kubernetes package manager. The project is capitalized as _Helm_; the CLI tool is lowercase `helm`.\n\n**Kube Config (KUBECONFIG)**\n\"The Helm client learns about Kubernetes clusters by using files in the _Kube config_ file format. By default, Helm attempts to find this file in the place where `kubectl` creates it (`$HOME/.kube/config`).\"\n\n**Lint (Linting)**\n\"To _lint_ a chart is to validate that it follows the conventions and requirements of the Helm chart standard.\"\n\n**Provenance (Provenance file)**\nProvenance files accompany charts, containing cryptographic hashes and signatures for security validation purposes.\n\n**Release**\n\"When a chart is installed, the Helm library creates a _release_ to track that installation.\"\n\n**Release Number (Release Version)**\n\"A sequential counter is used to track releases as they change\" through install, upgrade, and rollback operations.\n\n**Rendering Engine / Template Rendering Engine**\n*Not present in the glossary.*\n\n**Repository (Repo, Chart Repository)**\n\"Helm charts may be stored on dedicated HTTP servers called _chart repositories_ (_repositories_, or just _repos_).\"\n\n**Values (Values Files, values.yaml)**\n\"Values provide a way to override template defaults with your own information\" during installation or upgrade."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ba092422-5310-41aa-b517-7e6c04f864c8","uuid":"8e0b9c4a-8335-417b-9f12-b5ec9e6f68a3","timestamp":"2026-08-31T08:31:54.572Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":43990,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Glossary Terms from Helm Documentation\n\n**Chart**\n\"A Helm package that contains information sufficient for installing a set of Kubernetes resources into a Kubernetes cluster.\"\n\n**Chart Archive**\n\"A _chart archive_ is a tarred and gzipped (and optionally signed) chart.\"\n\n**Chart Dependency (Subcharts)**\nCharts may depend on other charts through soft dependencies (not requiring Helm tooling) or hard dependencies (bundled within the `charts/` directory and installed together).\n\n**Chart Version**\n\"Charts are versioned according to the [SemVer 2 spec](https://semver.org). A version number is required on every chart.\"\n\n**Chart.yaml**\n\"Information about a chart is stored in a special file called `Chart.yaml`. Every chart must have this file.\"\n\n**Helm (and helm)**\nHelm is the Kubernetes package manager. The project is capitalized as _Helm_; the CLI tool is lowercase `helm`.\n\n**Kube Config (KUBECONFIG)**\n\"The Helm client learns about Kubernetes clusters by using files in the _Kube config_ file format. By default, Helm attempts to find this file in the place where `kubectl` creates it (`$HOME/.kube/config`).\"\n\n**Lint (Linting)**\n\"To _lint_ a chart is to validate that it follows the conventions and requirements of the Helm chart standard.\"\n\n**Provenance (Provenance file)**\nProvenance files accompany charts, containing cryptographic hashes and signatures for security validation purposes.\n\n**Release**\n\"When a chart is installed, the Helm library creates a _release_ to track that installation.\"\n\n**Release Number (Release Version)**\n\"A sequential counter is used to track releases as they change\" through install, upgrade, and rollback operations.\n\n**Rendering Engine / Template Rendering Engine**\n*Not present in the glossary.*\n\n**Repository (Repo, Chart Repository)**\n\"Helm charts may be stored on dedicated HTTP servers called _chart repositories_ (_repositories_, or just _repos_).\"\n\n**Values (Values Files, values.yaml)**\n\"Values provide a way to override template defaults with your own information\" during installation or upgrade.","durationMs":6980,"url":"https://helm.sh/docs/glossary/"}}
